                    <history>
                        <origin>
                            <origDate>1487</origDate>
                        </origin>
                        <provenance>On ff. 21v and 22 are marginal notes by another hand dated as follows: '1492 die 8 martis', '1493 die 22 octobris. satis bene', '1490 die 31 martis satis bene', '1495 12 augusti. optime'. These entries seem to refer to the making of planetary sigils. At the back of the first fly-leaf the visiting card of Count Paolo Vimercati-Sozzi (1801-1883), the archaeologist, is pasted in.</provenance>
                        <acquisition>Purchased on 14th October 1910 from Rosenthal for £6. Accessioned on 10 December 1910.</acquisition>
